    "author_recorded_subject": "rpc: drain independent submissions through a bounded commit owner",
    "author_recorded_rationale": "rpc: drain independent submissions through a bounded commit owner\n\nKeep ordinary per-request fee bounds, authoritative admission, snapshot publication and validation barriers. Only sendrawtransaction opts in; producer threads perform their existing callback waits and relay after commit acknowledgment. Drain immediately with no collection timer, share cs_main across bounded slices, and retain direct fallback under overload. Wallet, Chronik and existing fair P2P admission remain direct/separate.\n\nAdd callback/snapshot causal control, independent exception and shutdown/byte-pressure cases, plus native concurrent-error/conflict and sequential-array functional coverage. Candidate compile/runtime validation pending coordinated build; no performance claim.\n\nCoordinator validated purpose integration (2026-10-21): includes original design46df, server-enabled lifetime fixupa422 and argv-only functional fixup4880. Retain full per-transaction authoritative admission/publication/callbacks; bounded immediate RPC-only commit owner, direct overload fallback, no P2P result flattening. Native-only functional enters with its real NativeMiniWallet/wallet-receive prerequisites. Typed outcome/barrier successor29736+d559 remains separate UNVALIDATED work and is excluded here.",
    "concrete_problem": "Independent unlocked RPC producers repeatedly acquire the commit lock; one bounded owner can drain immediate slices while preserving per-request policy/results and notification ordering.",
    "split_mechanism": "Standalone shared purpose; originaldesign46df+feature25a; a422serverlifecycle and4880argvfixups folded.",
